# Notification LED, flashlight and vibrator

## Find the LEDs

The kernel exposes every LED under `/sys/class/leds`. The notification
LED is an RGB LED; the flashlight is two white flash LEDs.

```elixir
leds = File.ls!("/sys/class/leds") |> Enum.sort()
```

A few helpers to read and write LED settings:

```elixir
defmodule Led do
  @root "/sys/class/leds"

  def find(pattern), do: Enum.find(File.ls!(@root), &String.contains?(&1, pattern))

  def read(led, file) do
    Path.join([@root, led, file]) |> File.read!() |> String.trim()
  end

  def write(led, file, value) do
    File.write(Path.join([@root, led, file]), to_string(value))
  end

  def max(led), do: led |> read("max_brightness") |> String.to_integer()
end

rgb = Led.find("rgb")
flash = Led.find("flash")
{rgb, flash}
```

## Notification LED

Set a colour with values from 0 to 255.

```elixir
set_color = fn {r, g, b} ->
  max = Led.max(rgb)
  scale = fn v -> div(v * max, 255) end
  Led.write(rgb, "multi_intensity", "#{scale.(r)} #{scale.(g)} #{scale.(b)}")
  Led.write(rgb, "brightness", max)
end

set_color.({255, 0, 0})
```

Cycle through a few colours, then switch it off:

```elixir
for color <- [{255, 0, 0}, {0, 255, 0}, {0, 0, 255}, {255, 255, 255}] do
  set_color.(color)
  Process.sleep(500)
end

Led.write(rgb, "brightness", 0)
```

## Flashlight

Writing a brightness turns the flash LED on in torch mode.

```elixir
Led.write(flash, "brightness", Led.max(flash))
Process.sleep(1_000)
Led.write(flash, "brightness", 0)
```

## Vibrator

The `rumble` tool plays one vibration: duration in milliseconds, then an
optional strength from 1 to 65535.

```elixir
System.cmd("rumble", ["300"])
```

A pattern:

```elixir
for ms <- [100, 100, 400] do
  System.cmd("rumble", [to_string(ms)])
  Process.sleep(150)
end
```
